  m_Name: Extensor_digitorum_digitalis_lateralis_muscle.R
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ModelPartDataSO
  id: Extensor_digitorum_digitalis_lateralis_muscle.R
  partName: Extensor_digitorum_digitalis_lateralis_muscle.R
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'This muscle assists in extending the lateral digits and supports overall limb
    stability. It works alongside the extensor digitorum communis to ensure proper
    extension and positioning of the toes. By contributing to balanced digit movement,
    it helps maintain stability during locomotion. '
  - It also plays a role in preventing excessive strain on individual digits. This
    muscle is important for coordinated movement and proper distribution of forces
    across the limb during weight-bearing activities.
